Fix flaky ralph session-budget-integration timeout test
────────────────────────────────────────
ULID:      01KJ8XM5X8S04X7DSDP9TQQ9XR
Slugs:     task-fix-flaky-ralph-budget-test
Type:      bug
Status:    pending_review
Priority:  2
Automation: eligible
Session:   01KJ8Z3Q4E9VDAF133VNS7YC9Q

─── Description ───
  The test 'should clean up budget.json after normal exit (max-iterations reached)' in tests/ralph/session-budget-integration.test.ts times out intermittently. The spawnRalphUntil helper has a 25s safety timeout that races against ralph completing a full iteration with the mock agent. Under CI load or during ralph loop, this timeout fires before ralph finishes. Possible approaches: increase timeout, optimize mock agent response time, or restructure to test cleanup without spawning full ralph subprocess.
Tags:      bug, testing, ralph
Created:   2026-02-24T22:51:55.176Z
Started:   2026-02-24T23:22:48.146Z

─── Notes ───
[2026-02-24T23:10:49.721Z] @claude:
Root cause: spawnRalphUntil and testSignalCleanup helpers used cwd: process.cwd() (real project root). When the real working tree had uncommitted changes, getWorkingTreeStatus() returned dirty, causing runWrapUpAgent() to spawn a wrap-up agent with a 2-minute timeout — well exceeding the test's 25s safety timeout. Fix: (1) Changed cwd to tempDir (in /tmp, outside any git repo), (2) Initialize a clean git repo in tempDir with initial commit so getWorkingTreeStatus() reliably returns clean, (3) This ensures isWrapUpNeeded() returns false and wrap-up is skipped. All 3513 tests pass.
[2026-02-24T23:18:54.260Z] @claude:

